{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification binds sensor states to safe and coverage-oriented actions, ensuring conservative obstacle recovery and steady exploration. Recovery states use directed turns or, as a last resort, a full scan. Exploration alternates between random_walk and short forward moves, with obstacle events triggering recovery before resuming exploration.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect hardware modularity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward in commit, directed turns in recovery, and full_rotate only after repeated blockages."
  ],
  "G": [
